// Repro (2026-11-19): a small, black, SOUNDING head on a chord's stem cannot be written.
// Kuecken Op.47-3 bar 70 (Fr. Kistner 1711): a two-note tremolo between a white chord and a white note; the chord's
// stem carries one more head, small and black, at the pitch of the tremolo's other end (gis' / e) -- read as that
// pitch struck once with the chord at the ffp, the tremolo then going between the chord and the note.
// The nearest the grammar has: the pitch inside the chord at full size (drawn white, sounding on every stroke).
// cue { } draws small notes but is silent and has a stem of its own; @notehead(...) changes the shape, not the size.
octave absolute
time 6/8
key b major
part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }
section A {
  rh {
    repeat tremolo 24 { <gis cis' gis'>64 gis'64 } |
  }
  lh {
    repeat tremolo 24 { <e, e>64 e64 } |
  }
}
score { staff rh staff lh }